      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3}{4}(2x-{x}^{2}),\\,0\\le x\\le 2.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{3}].$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the third raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{3}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}(2x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{4}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{10}{x}^{5}-\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{6})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3\\cdot {2}^{5}}{10}-\\frac{{2}^{6}}{8})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{5}-8 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
